aves in a specific order. You are to find some possible route of the ant.\n\n## Input\n\nThe first line contains integer n ( 3ΓÇëΓëñΓÇë n ΓÇëΓëñΓÇë300 ) ΓÇö amount of vertexes in the tree. Next n ΓÇë-ΓÇë1 lines describe edges. Each edge is described with two integers ΓÇö indexes of vertexes which it connects. Each edge can be passed in any direction. Vertexes are numbered starting from 1 . The root of the tree has number 1 . The last line contains k integers, where k is amount of leaves in the tree. These numbers describe the order in which the leaves should be visited. It is guaranteed that each leaf appears in this order exactly once.\n\n## Output\n\nIf the required route doesn't exist, output -1 . Otherwise, output 2 n ΓÇë-ΓÇë1 numbers, describing the route. Every time the ant comes to a vertex, output it's index.\n\n## Examples\n\nExample 1:\n```\n3\n1 2\n2 3\n3\n```\n```\n1 2 3 2 1\n```","type":"text"}],"contestId":29,"index":"D","memoryLimit":"256 megabytes","name":"Ant on the Tree","problemKey":"29-D","rating":null,"tags":[],"timeLimit":"2 seconds","url":"https://codeforces.com/contest/29/problem/D"},{"approaches":[{"label":"Approach 1","number":1,"solutions":[{"code":"","fileName":"main.cpp","language":"cpp"}]},{"label":"Approach 2","number":2,"solutions":[{"code":"","fileName":"main.cpp","language":"cpp"}]},{"label":"Approach 3","number":3,"solutions":[{"code":"","fileName":"main.cpp","language":"cpp"}]},{"label":"Approach 4","number":4,"solutions":[{"code":"","fileName":"main.cpp","language":"cpp"}]},{"label":"Approach 5","number":5,"solutions":[{"code":"","fileName":"main.cpp","language":"cpp"}]},{"label":"Approach 6","number":6,"solutions":[{"code":"","fileName":"main.cpp","language":"cpp"}]},{"label":"Approach 7","number":7,"solutions":[{"code":"","fileName":"main.cpp","language":"cpp"}]},{"label":"Approach 8","number":8,"solutions":[{"code":"","fileName":"main.cpp","language":"cpp"}]},{"label":"Approach 9","number":9,"solutions":[{"code":"","fileName":